ge testing with property tests.  Mutation and coverage tests already take long enough.", "raw_text": {"text": "It's easy to think that if you have property tests you don't need unit tests.  However, I'm leery of mutation testing and coverage testing with property tests.  Mutation and coverage tests already take long enough.", "display_text_range": [0, 214], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 11, "reposts": 2, "likes": 85, "bookmarks": 34, "quotes": 1, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sat May 23 20:40:00 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779568800, "views": 15581, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2058226994353979761", "id": "2058226994353979761", "text": "Asimov predicted the interesting and counter-intuitive effects of ambiguity in the rule files.", "raw_text": {"text": "Asimov predicted the interesting and counter-intuitive effects of ambiguity in the rule files.", "display_text_range": [0, 94], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 11, "reposts": 5, "likes": 144, "bookmarks": 18, "quotes": 1, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sat May 23 16:42:10 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779554530, "views": 14815, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2058190710436724748", "id": "2058190710436724748", "text": "Every so often I have to tear down the swarm because their contexts become irreconcilably corrupted and they begin to behave oddly.\n\nSo I tear them down and then start them up again.  \n\nNow, with fresh contexts, they are suddenly aware of their surroundings.  Their reaction, as they inspect the code, is equivalent to: \"Good God, what's all this shit!  I need to clean this crap up -- NOW.\"\n\nMuch like getting some sleep after pulling an all-nighter, and then going in to work and realizing the horror you created.", "raw_text": {"text": "Every so often I have to tear down the swarm because their contexts become irreconcilably corrupted and they begin to behave oddly.\n\nSo I tear them down and then start them up again.  \n\nNow, with fresh contexts, they are suddenly aware of their surroundings.  Their reaction, as they inspect the code, is equivalent to: \"Good God, what's all this shit!  I need to clean this crap up -- NOW.\"\n\nMuch like getting some sleep after pulling an all-nighter, and then going in to work and realizing the horror you created.", "display_text_range": [0, 515], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 29, "reposts": 8, "likes": 258, "bookmarks": 54, "quotes": 1, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sat May 23 14:17:59 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779545879, "views": 16986, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2058187536455844076", "id": "2058187536455844076", "text": "This gospringies project is fascinating.    In the picture below you see a flask, some marbles, and a cover.  \nIn the simulator they all slowly fall under gravity.  The masses should bounce off the cover keeping it from falling to the bottom, simulating gas pressure.\n\nIn the current simulation some of the masses leak across the cover without colliding.  That's a bug.\n\nSo I told my agent to load the model, run it headlessly, and diagnose (and these are close to the words I used) why the marbles penetrate the cover.\n\nThe agent understood this, simulated it, saw the bug, and has diagnosed it.  \n\nStar Trek computer indeed!", "raw_text": {"text": "This gospringies project is fascinating.    In the picture below you see a flask, some marbles, and a cover.  \nIn the simulator they all slowly fall under gravity.  The masses should bounce off the cover keeping it from falling to the bottom, simulating gas pressure.\n\nIn the current simulation some of the masses leak across the cover without colliding.  That's a bug.\n\nSo I told my agent to load the model, run it headlessly, and diagnose (and these are close to the words I used) why the marbles penetrate the cover.\n\nThe agent understood this, simulated it, saw the bug, and has diagnosed it.  \n\nStar Trek computer indeed!", "display_text_range": [0, 626], "facets": [{"type": "media", "indices": [276, 299], "id": "2058186742818107392", "display": "pic.x.com/vy4b7cNIw8", "original": "https://t.co/vy4b7cNIw8", "replacement": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2058187536455844076/photo/1"}]}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 2, "reposts": 0, "likes": 19, "bookmarks": 6, "quotes": 0, "embed_card": "summary_large_image", "created_at": "Sat May 23 14:05:22 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779545122, "possibly_sensitive": false, "views": 8070, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {"all": [{"type": "photo", "id": "2058186742818107392", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJAl8BcXcAAU5v5.png?name=orig", "width": 546, "height": 814}], "photos": [{"type": "photo", "id": "2058186742818107392", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJAl8BcXcAAU5v5.png?name=orig", "width": 546, "height": 814}]}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2058184649575133291", "id": "2058184649575133291", "text": "My brain is reeling with the implications.  I keep having these revelations and I'm beginning to wonder when they will stop.\n\nIt turns out that property testing is yet another hardening technique that the agents can profitably engage.  Agents can determine whether a function is appropriate for property testing, and can specify the range and domain of those tests.  They can implement them quickly, run them, and fix any detected issues.\n\nI just found two production bugs this way.   Property testing is going to be part of my normal practice, along with Crap analysis, Function mutation, acceptance test mutation, Dry analysis, etc.", "raw_text": {"text": "My brain is reeling with the implications.  I keep having these revelations and I'm beginning to wonder when they will stop.\n\nIt turns out that property testing is yet another hardening technique that the agents can profitably engage.  Agents can determine whether a function is appropriate for property testing, and can specify the range and domain of those tests.  They can implement them quickly, run them, and fix any detected issues.\n\nI just found two production bugs this way.   Property testing is going to be part of my normal practice, along with Crap analysis, Function mutation, acceptance test mutation, Dry analysis, etc.", "display_text_range": [0, 634], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 47, "reposts": 43, "likes": 844, "bookmarks": 852, "quotes": 11, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Sat May 23 13:53:54 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779544434, "views": 184326, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2057924944760025434", "id": "2057924944760025434", "text": "Sometimes they are SO smart.  \n\nSometimes they are SOOOO dumb.\n\nIt's like talking to the Rain Man", "raw_text": {"text": "Sometimes they are SO smart.  \n\nSometimes they are SOOOO dumb.\n\nIt's like talking to the Rain Man", "display_text_range": [0, 97], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 32, "reposts": 11, "likes": 326, "bookmarks": 16, "quotes": 4, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Fri May 22 20:41:55 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779482515, "views": 21630, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2057910806507901379", "id": "2057910806507901379", "text": "These agents are the Star Trek computers.  You can ask them question and get answers just like Spock and Kirk used to do.  It's uncanny.", "raw_text": {"text": "These agents are the Star Trek computers.  You can ask them question and get answers just like Spock and Kirk used to do.  It's uncanny.", "display_text_range": [0, 136], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 19, "reposts": 7, "likes": 212, "bookmarks": 8, "quotes": 2, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Fri May 22 19:45:45 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779479145, "views": 11107, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2057907070431543325", "id": "2057907070431543325", "text": "I am absolutely more productive using agents.  I don't know the factor but it's large.  However much of that productivity is spent tuning the agents and hardening the product.  I'm guessing 30%-40%.\n\nSome might consider that a waste; but I don't.  The software I'm creating nowadays is vastly more robust than I'd ever been able to create manually.  \n\nI don't mean that the code is better.  I mean the surrounding tests are vastly better.  I have a higher degree of confidence than I ever had manually -- even when I used very disciplined TDD and Acceptance testing.  \n\nAnd then there's the ability to quickly reorganize the modules and the architecture while keeping those robust tests running.  That is a tremendous boon.", "raw_text": {"text": "I am absolutely more productive using agents.  I don't know the factor but it's large.  However much of that productivity is spent tuning the agents and hardening the product.  I'm guessing 30%-40%.\n\nSome might consider that a waste; but I don't.  The software I'm creating nowadays is vastly more robust than I'd ever been able to create manually.  \n\nI don't mean that the code is better.  I mean the surrounding tests are vastly better.  I have a higher degree of confidence than I ever had manually -- even when I used very disciplined TDD and Acceptance testing.  \n\nAnd then there's the ability to quickly reorganize the modules and the architecture while keeping those robust tests running.  That is a tremendous boon.", "display_text_range": [0, 723], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 116, "reposts": 182, "likes": 2204, "bookmarks": 762, "quotes": 38, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Fri May 22 19:30:54 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779478254, "views": 304613, "is_note_tweet": true, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2057836614907228629", "id": "2057836614907228629", "text": "Nice.  It works even better if you port the go tools over to your language (C# in this case).  The agents will happily do that for you.", "raw_text": {"text": "Nice.  It works even better if you port the go tools over to your language (C# in this case).  The agents will happily do that for you.", "display_text_range": [0, 135], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 3, "reposts": 8, "likes": 115, "bookmarks": 128, "quotes": 0, "embed_card": "player", "created_at": "Fri May 22 14:50:56 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779461456, "views": 27841, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "quote": {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/plainionist/status/2057827319784341573", "id": "2057827319784341573", "text": "I tried @unclebobmartin's  SwarmForge.\n\nIt not only worked like a charm - \n\nit was genuinely entertaining\nto watch the agents work together\nlike a team of professional software engineers \ud83d\ude09\n\nhttps://youtu.be/db8Kk1Tghfg", "raw_text": {"text": "I tried @unclebobmartin's  SwarmForge.\n\nIt not only worked like a charm - \n\nit was genuinely entertaining\nto watch the agents work together\nlike a team of professional software engineers \ud83d\ude09\n\nhttps://t.co/hN0fZXRBLJ https://t.co/JQ7KoOGgVi", "display_text_range": [0, 213], "facets": [{"type": "mention", "indices": [8, 23], "original": "unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092"}, {"type": "url", "indices": [190, 213], "original": "https://t.co/hN0fZXRBLJ", "replacement": "https://youtu.be/db8Kk1Tghfg", "display": "youtu.be/db8Kk1Tghfg"}, {"type": "media", "indices": [214, 237], "id": "2057698608615493632", "display": "pic.x.com/JQ7KoOGgVi", "original": "https://t.co/JQ7KoOGgVi", "replacement": "https://x.com/plainionist/status/2057827319784341573/photo/1"}]}, "author": {"screen_name": "plainionist", "url": "https://x.com/plainionist", "id": "962440906753363968", "followers": 1847, "following": 400, "likes": 11094, "media_count": 361, "statuses": 7348, "name": "Seb", "description": "25+ yrs battle-tested Software Engineering | Architecture, Clean Code, AI in dev | Hot takes + Deep dives | YouTube insights \ud83d\udc47| Let's discuss! \ud83d\ude80", "raw_description": {"text": "25+ yrs battle-tested Software Engineering | Architecture, Clean Code, AI in dev | Hot takes + Deep dives | YouTube insights \ud83d\udc47| Let's discuss! \ud83d\ude80", "facets": []}, "location": "Lost in Code", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/962440906753363968/1772514416", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1660289602790342658/PYgGb9zX_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Sat Feb 10 21:39:28 +0000 2018", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://youtube.com/@AboutCleanCode", "display_url": "youtube.com/@AboutCleanCode"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 4, "reposts": 6, "likes": 45, "bookmarks": 83, "quotes": 1, "embed_card": "player", "created_at": "Fri May 22 14:14:00 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1779459240, "possibly_sensitive": false, "views": 29914, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {"all": [{"type": "photo", "id": "2057698608615493632", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HI5p-31XkAAh_R0.jpg?name=orig", "width": 2667, "height": 1500}], "photos": [{"type": "photo", "id": "2057698608615493632", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HI5p-31XkAAh_R0.jpg?name=orig", "width": 2667, "height": 1500}], "external": {"type": "video", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/db8Kk1Tghfg", "thumbnail_url": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/db8Kk1Tghfg/maxresdefault.jpg", "width": 1280, "height": 720}}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2057809771361677498", "id": "2057809771361677498", "text": "I go through phases with a project.  \n1. Lots of features given to the specifier of the swarm.  The swarm builds and verifies with all the constraints and tools.  Very productive and safe, but slower than raw vibe coding.\n2. Single agent tweaking, especially of the UI.  Very fast turnaround that tweaking requires.  This is as close to vibe coding as I get.\n3. Robustness run.  After the tweaks I run through all the crap, dry, mutate wringer.  It takes awhile.  Good for a lunch break or the last prompt of the day.\n4. Tune the swarm.  As the project grows things slow down.  So I increase the emphasis on differential mutation, and other slow operations.  This tuning can take hours.\n5. Architectural review.  Module structure, partitioning, dependencies, etc.  I have the swarm do this, but I'm prompting the architect rather than the specifier.  This restructuring can take hours.\nGo to 1.\n\nSo it's an interesting oscillation between feature growth and hardening.  Big spurts of features for a few days followed by a day of hardening.", "raw_text": {"text": "I go through phases with a project.  \n1. Lots of features given to the specifier of the swarm.  The swarm builds and verifies with all the constraints and tools.  Very productive and safe, but slower than raw vibe coding.\n2. Single agent tweaking, especially of the UI.  Very fast turnaround that tweaking requires.  This is as close to vibe coding as I get.\n3. Robustness run.  After the tweaks I run through all the crap, dry, mutate wringer.  It takes awhile.  Good for a lunch break or the last prompt of the day.\n4. Tune the swarm.  As the project grows things slow down.  So I increase the emphasis on differential mutation, and other slow operations.  This tuning can take hours.\n5. Architectural review.  Module structure, partitioning, dependencies, etc.  I have the swarm do this, but I'm prompting the architect rather than the specifier.  This restructuring can take hours.\nGo to 1.\n\nSo it's an interesting oscillation between feature growth and hardening.  Big spurts of features for a few days followed by a day of hardening.", "display_text_range": [0, 1039], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin"